WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.643 --> 00:00:03.181
- The most recognizable thing in the sky,

00:00:03.181 --> 00:00:05.699
is obviously the
silhouette of the Spitfire.

00:00:05.699 --> 00:00:07.640
She's just a beautiful lady, I assure

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.559
a lot of men would like
to actually marry her.

00:00:09.559 --> 00:00:12.559
I'm sure their wives wouldn't agree.

00:00:13.607 --> 00:00:18.364
There's 396 parts in the Spitfire
seat, how do I know that?

00:00:18.364 --> 00:00:19.281
I built it.

00:00:25.605 --> 00:00:27.405
- [Narrator] This is Martin Phillips.

00:00:27.405 --> 00:00:29.528
- My name is Martin Phillips, and I am

00:00:29.528 --> 00:00:32.724
sitting next to my Spitfire RR232

00:00:32.724 --> 00:00:35.931
which I'm the proud owner of.

00:00:35.931 --> 00:00:38.981
- [Narrator] Martin is
obsessed with Spitfires.

00:00:38.981 --> 00:00:39.939
- [Announcer] The big bombers

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.185
join in pounding the shoreline.

00:00:42.185 --> 00:00:44.366
- [Narrator] In the darkest
days of World War II,

00:00:44.366 --> 00:00:47.625
Spitfires filled the skies above England.

00:00:47.625 --> 00:00:50.958
They are an icon, like freedom on wings.

00:00:51.987 --> 00:00:54.686
British kids make models of them.

00:00:54.686 --> 00:00:56.004
But Martin took his Spitfire

00:00:56.004 --> 00:00:58.671
devotion to a whole other level.

00:00:59.529 --> 00:01:02.127
For his 40th birthday, Martin's friends

00:01:02.127 --> 00:01:05.333
gave him a single Spitfire rivet.

00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:07.232
- When I was presented with this rivet,

00:01:07.232 --> 00:01:09.717
the challenge was to go and
build myself a Spitfire,

00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:11.792
so on the spar of the
moment, not thinking, I said,

00:01:11.792 --> 00:01:13.392
“Why, I'll go out on a Monday morning

00:01:13.392 --> 00:01:15.472
and I will build a Spitfire."

00:01:15.472 --> 00:01:17.051
I never thought that over a period

00:01:17.051 --> 00:01:20.395
of 14 years, I'd had
probably wear three cars out

00:01:20.395 --> 00:01:21.952
with mileage, along the journey

00:01:21.952 --> 00:01:25.253
to provide all the parts
that you now see today.

00:01:25.253 --> 00:01:28.549
The fuel tanks, they came
from Norway and Sweden.

00:01:28.549 --> 00:01:30.555
Some of the other parts came from Russia,

00:01:30.555 --> 00:01:32.475
some of the parts came from Israel,

00:01:32.475 --> 00:01:37.115
some of the other parts came
from Holland, came from France.

00:01:37.115 --> 00:01:39.254
One of the wings was offered to us

00:01:39.254 --> 00:01:42.229
through a lost property department.

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:45.732
And another wing came from a
little guy coming into work.

00:01:45.732 --> 00:01:49.216
He said, "I got a Spitfire
wing in my garden."

00:01:49.216 --> 00:01:51.776
The man hours that go
into a project like this,

00:01:51.776 --> 00:01:55.958
don't underestimate it, they are terrific

00:01:55.958 --> 00:01:58.993
and I know the blood, sweat
and tears that went into that.

00:01:58.993 --> 00:02:02.054
After 14 years, I know the
questions you're gonna ask me,

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:03.653
“Do you fly it?"

00:02:03.653 --> 00:02:05.174
Sadly, not.

00:02:05.174 --> 00:02:06.854
I am learning to fly and I hope,

00:02:06.854 --> 00:02:09.857
one day to fly it, but
greater guys than me fly it.

00:02:09.857 --> 00:02:14.045
- My name's Matt Jones,
I'm a Spitfire pilot.

00:02:14.045 --> 00:02:17.977
The modern airliners fly
85% the speed of sound,

00:02:17.977 --> 00:02:22.144
they've got Spitfires flying
at 96, 97% the speed of sound.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.560
You don't get in a
Spitfire, you strap it on

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.977
and it becomes a part of you.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.777
Because the airplane means
so much to so many people,

00:02:33.777 --> 00:02:35.938
there are a lot of people who have

00:02:35.938 --> 00:02:39.192
gone down Martin's path
and started thinking

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.673
they wanna build a Spitfire.

00:02:41.673 --> 00:02:45.894
But I've never met anyone
else whose completed it.

00:02:45.894 --> 00:02:48.815
He dedicated his life to
finding the parts he needed

00:02:48.815 --> 00:02:51.499
to get this airplane flying again.

00:02:51.499 --> 00:02:53.119
- I went through these 14 years,

00:02:53.119 --> 00:02:55.435
had heartache when bits didn't fit.

00:02:55.435 --> 00:02:57.083
Just putting it together and finishing it,

00:02:57.083 --> 00:02:58.518
and the providence and the journey,

00:02:58.518 --> 00:03:00.880
the journey I went on, you know, tears.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.823
Even today, I cry when it runs.

00:03:03.823 --> 00:03:07.406
It's just been amazing,
absolutely amazing.

